# Test: fib kernel alone (without fib vpp) is refused under interface backend vpp.
# Question: does `ze config validate` refuse `fib kernel` with no `fib vpp`
#           block under `interface backend vpp`, naming `fib kernel` and the
#           fix `set fib vpp`?
#           A unit test cannot prove `fib-kernel`'s `HostSideDataPlane` and
#           `fib-vpp`'s `ProgramsFIB` registrations combine inside `ze config
#           validate` to derive `set fib vpp` from the registry.
# VALIDATES: spec-dataplane-compatibility-guard AC-14 (P-1b) -- a host-side
#            FIB writer of another plane alone under VPP leaves VPP's FIB with
#            no route, so it is refused with `set fib vpp`.
# PREVENTS: a VPP router with only `fib kernel` committing silently and leaving
#           VPP's forwarding table empty.
stdin=config:terminator=EOF_CONF
interface {
	backend vpp;
}
fib {
	kernel {
	}
}
EOF_CONF

cmd=foreground:seq=1:exec=ze config validate -:stdin=config
expect=exit:code=1
expect=stdout:contains=fib kernel
expect=stdout:contains=set fib vpp
